  "final_answer_preview": "'Dishonestly' is defined in Section 2(7) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, as doing anything with the intention of causing wrongful gain to one person or wrongful loss to another person. This definition is illustrated in various sections, such as in Section 303(1) where an act of taking an article without consent for personal gain is considered dishonest and constitutes theft. Additionally, Section 335 outlines that making a false document with dishonest intent also falls under this definition. The concept of dishonesty is further exemplified in Section 318(1) where deception is used to induce another party to part with property, and in Section 334, which addresses breaking open a receptacle with dishonest intent.",
